# The program saves its headless window's first frame as Frame.pam; every
# tier must rasterize the same bytes. The SHA-256 is that of the clear and
# three rectangles under core.ui's one blend rule, computed apart from Jet:
# each color premultiplies on entry, (c * a + 127) / 255, and each byte,
# alpha included, becomes s + (d * (255 - a) + 127) / 255. The frame ends
# opaque, so its straight bytes are the canvas's.
step: built
stdout: = DrawCanvas.out
file: Frame.pam sha256 = "afe46603a5d6d82778a8d2e4a680182467a3a1b07b8df563446494f0836ed374"
